                                                                                
 Usage: opentide new rule [OPTIONS]                                             
                                                                                
 Scaffold a detection rule.                                                     
                                                                                
╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ --name             <str>     Object name; the filename is its slug           │
│ --platform         PLATFORM  Add a configuration block for this platform     │
│                              (repeatable): sentinel, splunk, crowdstrike,    │
│                              defender_for_endpoint, sentinel_one,            │
│                              carbon_black_cloud, harfanglab, elastic, sysdig │
│ --objective        <str>     UUID of the objective this rule implements      │
│                              (detection_model)                               │
│ --path             <str>     File to write, or a folder to write it in       │
│                              (default: the family's objects folder)          │
│ --help                       Show this message and exit.                     │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

 Examples
   $ opentide new rule --name "Suspicious LSASS Access" --platform sentinel --objective <objective-uuid>
